{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/961767-horror-combat","id":961767,"title":"Horror Combat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-01T10:30:39-07:00","id":961767,"title":"Horror Combat","content":"Have looked through quite a bit of threads and I can't seem to find what I'm looking for. As a disclaimer, I use spirit rules to determine stats/health/etc of Horrors because I felt the lack of concrete answer on if they were true spirits or just dream formed beasts was confusing. Besides all that, here is the question...<br /> <br /> How do you handle the concept of &quot;merging&quot; with your horror when opening up a gateway to defend yourself? I have a social character in my campaign who I surprised with a Beast change. (its a sort of crossover origin mundane humans turn supernatural sort of thing so I made up rules for how the transition would occur) This particular character chose a Phoenix like creature for her horror and decided that the lower her satiety the more it looks like a full blown phoenix and the higher her satiety the more it looks like a hybrid girl/phoenix more akin to a harpy (10 is basically just a sleeping girl).<br /> <br /> By default, beast's don't really have any ranged attacks or natural weapons. All of those are covered by atavisms. Well, she recently opened a gateway wanting to get more combat capable (generally shes all social) and was a little disappointed by the fact that she by default wasn't able to perform any ranged actions short of using the shotgun she was ill trained with while flying around a little.<br /> <br /> The other confusion is, Do they fully become a horror? Like, what determines if they even can grip a weapon? Are they a hybrid mixing of the Horror and Beast? If they are a Cerberus like creature then it wouldn't make sense for them to suddenly have arms. Is beast just a game where there are too many possibilities to cover and it ends up being very heavy on DM fiat?<br /> <br /> Currently I am contemplating either allowing any beast who is merged with their horror to do a 0L (lethal as a base regardless) melee or ranged attack using Brawl+Power (Melee) or Athletics+Finesse (Ranged). I am also contemplating making natural weapon fighting styles for ranged and melee beasts that are based on developing or justifying the power of natural weapons. Or just allow them to spend the attribute points for their horror they get from their lair trait and spend them on developing natural weapons.<br /> <br /> In the end, I'd just hate to limit players to using dragons breath or lightning strikes for ranged combat. If someone wants to make a pseudo porcupine horror I want them to be able to shoot quills at people to deal dmg. I'm just not entirely sure how to properly/consistently limit it to be fair to all concepts.<br /> <br /> Thanks for any advice or feedback. Sorry if my post seems a little all over the place. Wondering how others have handled this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 09-01-2016, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T14:00:49-07:00","id":961890,"title":"","content":"Hmm, well others may be able to give you something more system specific but I feel like an important aspect of consideration is missing here. A beast doesn't just have a lair, in a certain sense it IS it's lair. Think of it as much as part of its stomach or as any other part of its body (hence why it feeds better there). If your character is a pheonix, I can only imagine they chose at least one trait involving fire. Why is it necessary for it to have a ranged attack when it could literally call down an entire realm of fire onto the current scene? Fire that it would be immune to. I think the idea with Beast and the Primordial Pathway systems is Beasts should always have the home turf advantage. If you don't, run until you do. It makes considerations about WHERE you're fighting your enemy just as important as the 'how' or 'with what'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10415-vermillionde","name":"VermillionDe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T06:31:11-07:00","id":962221,"title":"","content":"Believe it or not, Fire was planned to be her 3rd lair trait after she bumped her lair to two. Without going super far into the back story there were two other lair traits that were more personal to the character. Combat wasn't the goal with the character but I think she would have liked a sort of razor feather ranged attack or a small fire bolt or something she could use as a single target basic attack.<br /> <br /> Also, there is one thing about the fire lair trait people may miss. You choose the size and potency of the flame when u first learn the trait and cannot change it afterwards. What this means is if you want to be able to turn the room into a blazing inferno and that is essentially how your lair is, then that is how its going to manifest every time. Meaning if you have allies and want to invoke the fire lair trait while in beast form u are suddenly cooking your entire team. The only place it states a beast can control who is affected by their tilts is in their lair. So it's likely that in anything but a solo campaign the character is going to pick a less intense flame.<br /> <br /> I think im beginning to see that beasts are basically intended to fight entirely using tilts and atavism while in their lair. While they are beasts of legends they use their environment far more than their body. Of course the beast could build themselves as a combat junkie and be scarey in melee as always that takes alot of investment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 09-02-2016, 09:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T00:05:13-07:00","id":963115,"title":"","content":"Atavisms can be reskinned to cover other concepts. Dragon's Breath is the quintessential flame attack, but there's nothing preventing it from being ice, acid, or electric breath with the same base rules just tweaked to reflect other elements. Your example porcupine is a little further off the base concept but I see no reason the same mechanics couldn't apply. At its core it's a very basic, abstracted ranged attack that could apply to a loooot of concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T00:38:22-07:00","id":963121,"title":"","content":"One advantage you get when you merge with the Horror is that you always test with the highest of a given type of Attribute (Power, Finesse, Resistance) due to the way the Horror's simplified Attributes work. For equipment, I would simply run it that it can be used fine and has the same mechanical effects as before, but visually it becomes incorporated into the Horror. A shotgun blast becomes a slew of razor-edged feathers flung from the phoenix's wings, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T10:30:33-07:00","id":964374,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the responses. ajf115, I really like your idea that the blending of beast and horror incorporates both organic as well as inorganic matter into itself. Means a heavily armored beast becomes a heavily armored horror with the armor reshaped to fit the new form and the weapons shifting into various forms of horrific natural weapons if they no longer have a means of operating said equipment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T10:41:58-07:00","id":964386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/961767-horror-combat?p=964374#post964374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the responses. ajf115, I really like your idea that the blending of beast and horror incorporates both organic as well as inorganic matter into itself. Means a heavily armored beast becomes a heavily armored horror with the armor reshaped to fit the new form and the weapons shifting into various forms of horrific natural weapons if they no longer have a means of operating said equipment.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I say, bringing the Dream into reality means bringing dream logic into play. The only issue I can see, mechanically speaking, is that you can't really disarm a phoenix of its feathers as easily as you can a person of a shotgun. You might simply make that the rule, though, and keep it as an advantage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T14:10:40-07:00","id":964508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/961767-horror-combat#post961767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By default, beast's don't really have any ranged attacks or natural weapons. All of those are covered by atavisms.</div> </div> </div> </div> Or Nightmares. Or guns. Or throwing things with Strength boosts. Or how about archery? Another fun thing is to go full on-support and buff others who do the attacking and you don't have to. Or there's always retainer swarms. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like, what determines if they even can grip a weapon? </div> </div> </div> Discussion between player and ST, that's what determines it. When you merge with your Horror, you basically merge minds inside of the Horror's body. But given that the player determines what the Horror looks like, they basically get to say if they have hands that can grip objects or not. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the end, I'd just hate to limit players to using dragons breath or lightning strikes for ranged combat. If someone wants to make a pseudo porcupine horror I want them to be able to shoot quills at people to deal dmg. I'm just not entirely sure how to properly/consistently limit it to be fair to all concepts. </div> </div> </div> Then have the PC train up firearms. Or any of the other ways to be able to deal damage. There's several social-based damaging powers out there, including the Siren's Voice Atavism and several Nightmare abilities. If you want to shoot quills, then reskin an existing power, or write up a new one - its not like we've covered every concievable power in just the core book, there's more that's coming. But there are lots of existing ways to have the characters involved in combat, no matter the focus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T13:17:05-07:00","id":968106,"title":"","content":"Yea, this topic seems to be confirming the concept of if a player wants something then they need to invest in it. A Horror isnt just going to have a means of natural attack unless they choose a existing atavism that does that or works with me to reskin/homebrew one that does what they want. Honestly, it seems like a simple thing now that my perspective has shifted, thanks everyone.<br /> <br /> About the only question id have left deals with scope. (Which I already have a good idea of but want to see what others think.) Homebrewing new abilities for things such as werewolves or vampires can be a little tricky in the fact that you don't suddenly want to create a ability that steps too much on a niche that another core supernatural has. You also need to make sure you don't create any abilities that trivialize/contradict the core themes of a splat. With Beasts, this seems like its really damn hard to do. I mean, Beasts as a concept are veerrrry broad. Would everyone agree that nearly any creature of legend or mythology or randomly spawned from a players brain is encouraged as a theme for beast provided it's reliant on fear and nightmares?<br /> <br /> A better way to ask maybe. Is there really any style of supernatural ability that would seem unfitting or outside the scope of Beast? I mean, provided they are balanced/toned down to match a comparable strength to other atavism/nightmares.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 09-12-2016, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T22:38:35-07:00","id":968379,"title":"","content":"I'd let the player attack using Power + Finesse, with the attack being Bashing damage or Lethal depending on whether the character does something like hit a target with a wing or attack a target with talons or beak. I base that off of the rules of page 188 for Ephemeral beings Combat. I figure that's fine as a simple base line and it's supported by the rules.<br /> <br /> If the player wants better damaging attacks, they can pick up the Limb From Limb Atavism or whatever else that they like. But I see nothing at all which says that a Horror can't do any attacks without an Atavism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}